<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<TimeML xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="TimeML_1.2.1.xsd">
  <DOCID>CURATION_USER</DOCID>
  <TIMEX3 tid="t0" type="DATE" value="2018-12-21T00:00:00" functionInDocument="CREATION_TIME" temporalFunction="false">2018-12-21</TIMEX3>
  <TEXT>A 54-year-old female patient was <EVENT eid="e1" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">admitted</EVENT> to our surgical department with a <TIMEX3 tid="t1" type="DURATION" value="P2M" temporalFunction="false">2 mo</TIMEX3> history of decreased <EVENT eid="e2" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">appetite</EVENT>, <EVENT eid="e3" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">nausea</EVENT>, <EVENT eid="e4" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">vomiting</EVENT>, and weight <EVENT eid="e5" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">loss</EVENT>, which <EVENT eid="e6" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">progressed</EVENT> to <EVENT eid="e7" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">difficulty</EVENT> in feeding <TIMEX3 tid="t2" type="DURATION" value="P2D" temporalFunction="false">3 d</TIMEX3> prior to her <EVENT eid="e8" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">visit</EVENT>. According to her medical <EVENT eid="e9" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">history</EVENT>, she was <EVENT eid="e10" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">diagnosed</EVENT> with refractory <EVENT eid="e11" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">ITP</EVENT> [<EVENT eid="e12" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">platelets</EVENT> (<EVENT eid="e13" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">PLT</EVENT>), 3000-8000/μL] <TIMEX3 tid="t3" type="DATE" value="2008" temporalFunction="false">10 years ago</TIMEX3>. After <EVENT eid="e14" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">admission</EVENT>, the patient underwent a <EVENT eid="e15" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">splenectomy</EVENT> and a distal subtotal <EVENT eid="e16" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">gastrectomy</EVENT> (D2 radical <EVENT eid="e17" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">resection</EVENT>) with Roux-en-Y reconstruction simultaneously. She had an uneventful <TIMEX3 tid="t4" type="DATE" value="X" temporalFunction="true" comment="e3c:timex3Class=PREPOSTEXP; e3c:value=NO_VALUE">postoperative</TIMEX3> <EVENT eid="e18" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">course</EVENT> with a slight <EVENT eid="e19" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">increase</EVENT> in her PLT <EVENT eid="e20" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">count</EVENT>. This <EVENT eid="e21" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">case</EVENT> is <EVENT eid="e22" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">unique</EVENT> in terms of the patient's <EVENT eid="e23" class="OCCURRENCE" comment="e3c:permanence=FINITE">complication</EVENT> of severe and medically refractory ITP.&#13;
</TEXT>
